<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nendrum Monastery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nendrum is an early Christian monastic site on Mahee Island in Strangford Lough, County Down, Northern Ireland, traditionally founded by Saint Mochaoi in the 5th century. Its remains include three concentric stone enclosures, the stump of a round tower and a church. Excavations found a tide mill dated to around 619, among the oldest known in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nendrum-monastery.jpg" alt="Nendrum Monastery" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pulsar.co.nr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nendrummonastery.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
